The vulnerability is about "parsing does not stop on a lone tag escape in the C file". This is likely a known CVE in irssi. Let me search for the specific vulnerability. The description mentions "lone tag escape" - this could be related to the `%` character in theme files. Let me look at the `theme_format_append_next` function more carefully:

```c
chr = **format;
if ((chr == '$' || chr == '%') &&
    (*format)[1] == '\0') {
    /* last char, always append */
    g_string_append_c(str, chr);
    (*format)++;
    return;
}
```

This handles the case where `$` or `%` is the last character. But what about when `%` is followed by something? Let me look at the code path:

```c
if (**format == '%') {
    /* format */
    (*format)++;
    if (**format != '{' && **format != '}') {
        chr = **format;
        ...
        (*format)++;
        return;
    }
    ...
}
```

